{
  "title": "THA Pseudotumor (Metal on Metal Reactions)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/422822/tha-pseudotumor-metal-on-metal-reactions",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 5 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A metal-on-metal (MoM) THA pseudotumor, also known as aseptic lymphocyte-dominant vasculitis-associated lesion (ALVAL), is a mass-forming tissue reaction caused by metal-on-metal wear",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/picture5.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis involves obtain meta-subtraction MRI studies in the setting of elevated serum metal ion levels (cobalt, chromium)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is typically revision arthroplasty for symptomatic pseudotumor with elevated metal ions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "10-15% of patients with MoM THA have a pseudotumor",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "45-50% of revisions in patients with MoM THA are due to pseudotumor or adverse local tissue reaction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elevated cobalt and chromium levels",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "female gender",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "high acetabulum inclination angle > 55°",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "two different mechanisms have been proposed for formation of pseudotumors:",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hypersensitivity to metal ions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "local high wear debris",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "variability in distribution of metal debris, degree of necrosis, and number, type, and arrangement of inflammatory cells",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "macrophages and lymphocytes are present in all cases with **lymphocytes** being predominant",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "patient's with high wear have more macrophages than those with primarily hypersensitivity to metal ions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patients with extensive infiltrates of macrophages tend to have smaller lymphocytic aggregates.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patient may complain of gradual onset of symptoms or a sudden inciting pain in the groin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common symptoms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be asymptomatic",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "groin pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "trendelenburg gait",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical Exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "soft tissue masses around the hip may be present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually normal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "groin pain with flexion, IR and adduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "groin pain with rising from a chair",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP pelvis, AP and lateral of affected hip",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "will show metal-on-metal THA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/mom_tha..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "necessary to rule out peri-prosthetic fractures as source of pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may show peri-prosthetic bony erosion, commonly seen in calcar region",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**MRI with Metal Artifact Reduction Sequence (MARS)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/pseudotumor..jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "normal radiographs in the setting of elevated metal ion levels (cobalt, chromium)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a pseudotumor will appear like a fluid collection or solid mass in periprosthetic soft tissues",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "T1 weighted images will show signal similar to bladder contents (transudate)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "T2 weighted images will generally show hyperintensity as compared to muscle and may be heterogenous or homogenous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/picture2.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/picture1.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "the hypointense content observed in T2 sequences may be related to the presence of necrosis or metal deposition",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Serum labs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "WBC, ESR and CRP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "metal ion levels (**cobalt, chromium)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "serum metal ion concentration highest at 12-24 months following index surgery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "correlates with the initial \"wear in\" or \"run-in\" phase of increased particle generation, but then followed by a \"steady state\" phase of decreased particle generation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "values **> 7 parts per billion** (ppb, or ug/L) generally an indication for advanced imaging with MRI",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Invasive studies",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Hip aspiration",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "synovial fluid analysis will allow for differentiation of a metallosis from periprosthetic infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "gross appearance of metallosis generally described as \"**dishwater fluid**\" with watery, grayish and hazy appearance",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/picture3.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "manual cell count necessary",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**fibrinous debris from metal-on-metal reactions will falsely elevate automated cell counts**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "well functioning THA with low metal ions and no pseudotumor on MRI",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "studies show that around 40% of patients with a pseudotumor are asymptomatic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "revision THA to ceramic-on-polyethelyne components",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422822/images/picture4.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "painful metal on metal THA, elevated metal ions, pseudotumor on MRI",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "rate of revision THA due to symptomatic pseudotumor is only 1.7–5.6%",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "most patients with pain, elevated ions or a psudotumor on MRI require operative intervention",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "significant bone loss, soft tissue destruction, degree of abductor muscle deficiency and poorlocal environment for healing corresponds to difficulty of revision and functional outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "if severely compromised abductor function or damaged soft-tissue affects implant stability, may require the use of a contrained liner",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "gluteus maximus transfer can be used to reconstruct deficient abductor mechanism",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "-1",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "higher rates of dislocation and infection",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Observation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "in the asymptomatic patient, serial hip radiographs to assess for wear, or component loosening can be performed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Revision THA to ceramic-on-polyethelyne components**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "depends on location of tumor and surgeon preferene",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "direct lateral and direct anterior commonly cited",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be single stage or 2 stages depending on surgeon preference or presence/concern of infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "depend on bone loss, abductor defiency and soft tissue damage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "constraint liners may be required if severe abductor deficiency is present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "complications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "instability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "deep infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "aseptic loosening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "persistent iliopsoas tendonitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "persistent metal related reaction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Repeat revision THA**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "14-20% of revision THAs performed due to a MoM pseudotumor require a 2nd operation within 5 years",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "revision THA to address reason for repeat failure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Pseudotumor induced femoral nerve palsy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rare, only case reports noted",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decompression and revision THA to ceramic-on polyethelyne components",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
